--- !u!114 &846837228
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 846837226}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3ff6acaa8b9f1994499dd387e6188532, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Comments: "This scene provides a basic setup for audio-reactive behaviors. First,
    the AudioTrack component provides an AudioSource, which may be pre-recorded audio
    or configured for live input using a microphone or global game audio. \n\nAudioSpectrum
    is then used to prepare the audio sampling data for analysis. AudioSample components
    use this data to isolate specific frequencies which can then be mapped to animate
    properties.\n\nAudioReactive components may then be used to animate properties
    using data provided by AudioSample. Each AudioSample may be referenced by as
    many AudioReactive components as needed, optimizing audio processing so that
    each frequency range is only calculated once per update.\n\nDuplicate this scene
    as a quick setup to create your own audio-reactive setup and modified to fit
    your needs. \n\nNote that sampling parameters will need to be adjusted to work
    with different audio since frequency ranges and amplitudes can widely vary."
  Warning: 
  URLTitle: Audio Documentation
  URL: https://axongenesis.gitbook.io/timeflow/reference/behaviors/audio
  URL2Title: 
  URL2: 
